Embedded fonts
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source tree and every compiled binary contain four typefaces from the Noto
family, which are NOT covered by the licences above:

    assets/fonts/NotoSans-Regular.ttf
    assets/fonts/NotoSans-Bold.ttf
    assets/fonts/NotoSans-Italic.ttf
    assets/fonts/NotoSansMono-Regular.ttf

They are Copyright the Noto Project Authors, licensed under the SIL Open Font
License, Version 1.1. The full text is at assets/fonts/LICENSE-Noto.txt and must
travel with any redistribution of the source or of a built binary.

The OFL permits bundling the fonts inside software and selling that software; it
does not permit selling the fonts on their own. That is the only obligation this
adds over the MIT/Apache terms, and nothing here does it.

Why they are embedded rather than loaded: asking the operating system what fonts
exist goes through fontconfig, whose first call can cost more than this program's
entire startup. See src/text.rs.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Colour emoji
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No emoji font is embedded or redistributed. At runtime the program opens a colour
emoji font already installed on the machine -- Noto Color Emoji on Linux, Apple
Color Emoji on macOS -- read-only, from a fixed list of absolute paths, and only
if a document turns out to contain an emoji. Nothing is copied and nothing is
shipped. See src/emoji.rs.

